diff --git a/docs/live-games.md b/docs/live-games.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f6243e2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/live-games.md
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+# Live games
+
+## Running and playing
+
+`bin/serve` builds the locked Rust dependencies offline in release mode and
+executes the server. All persistent data remains in `storage/quizzy.sqlite3`.
+The QR implementation is a cached Rust crate; no QR service, CDN, or frontend
+package install is required. The existing environment variables and moderator
+HTTP Basic login are unchanged. `/up` only becomes available after schema setup.
+
+On a quiz page, **Start a game** creates an independent run and opens
+`/moderate/games/<code>`. The moderator shares the displayed full HTTP URL or its
+QR code. Phones use `/play/<code>` without authentication. Start → Finish → Next
+(or End quiz on the last question) advances the game. An empty active-question
+set ends cleanly when Start is pressed.
+
+## Data and correctness
+
+- Each game snapshots the quiz title and ordered active questions at creation.
+  Edits, reordering, deactivation, or deletion of the original quiz cannot change
+  a running game. Subsequent runs use fresh snapshots. Game snapshots and their
+  history are retained independently of source quiz deletion.
+- `games` stores the phase, current question position, and transition version.
+  `players` is keyed by game and browser token; `answers` is keyed by game,
+  player, and question position. Updating an answer replaces that single row.
+- A 256-bit random HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookie under `/play` remembers the
+  browser for one year. Membership is still separate per game. Opening the same
+  link again resumes the original player; a new game asks for a new name.
+  Duplicate display names are allowed. Clearing cookies creates a new identity.
+- Moderator commands require Basic authentication, the existing secret-derived
+  CSRF token, the expected transition version, and a valid command for the
+  current phase. Old or duplicate commands return 409, not a second transition.
+- Player POSTs require the browser's CSRF token. Answer writes validate
+  membership, open phase, question position, and option bounds under the same
+  database mutex used for Finish. A delayed answer cannot affect a later
+  question, and an answer arriving after Finish is rejected.
+- Public responses are constructed explicitly, not serialized from the question
+  model. Open questions contain option text only: no correctness flags, results,
+  future questions, or moderator token. Unjoined clients receive no question
+  data. Once closed, the current question's correct options and the player's
+  result are available. Any marked-correct choice counts as correct.
+- The QR is an SVG encoding exactly the displayed full HTTP join URL, derived
+  from the request Host. It has the standard four-module white quiet zone and
+  is served only in the authenticated moderator area. All user strings are
+  escaped in HTML or inserted with DOM textContent. The existing CSP applies.
+
+## Live protocol and conference Wi-Fi
+
+The client maintains one outstanding long-poll `GET .../state?since=<cursor>`.
+The server waits asynchronously for a watch-channel change, or returns a
+heartbeat snapshot after ten seconds. No database lock or blocking worker is
+held while waiting. The browser re-renders only changed state and preserves
+partially typed names. Network errors use exponential backoff with jitter,
+explicit reconnect messaging, and a request timeout. Ended pages stop polling.
+
+There are separate notification channels for moderator counters and game
+phases. Answers and joins wake moderator screens, **not every other phone**;
+phase changes wake phones immediately. The answer POST itself returns the
+answerer's authoritative state. This avoids quadratic phone traffic as an
+entire audience votes. Rapid taps are serialized, retaining the latest queued
+choice so a slow first submission does not silently discard the last tap.
+
+Counters treat a player as present for 35 seconds after their last heartbeat,
+join, or answer. Thus transient Wi-Fi gaps do not immediately remove a player.
+Departures appear on the moderator's next heartbeat after that grace period
+(up to about 45 seconds after the last activity); returning phones restore their
+presence automatically. During an open question, both the numerator and
+denominator count present players. Closed-question option totals include all
+saved answers, including answers from players who subsequently disconnected.
+No saved membership or answers are deleted when presence expires.
+
+Notifications are hints only: SQLite is authoritative. A client can reconnect
+after missed updates or a process restart and receive the latest complete state.
+Revision numbers start from epoch microseconds on startup to prevent clients
+from rejecting post-restart snapshots as older than the previous process.
+Player poll cursors are separate from the shared response ordering revision.
+
+The implementation targets a single Rust process with a serialized SQLite
+connection, matching `bin/serve`. The role-specific watch channels are global
+within that process; a phase transition in another game may cause an extra
+heartbeat response, but never discloses that game's data. Horizontal deployment
+would require shared cross-process notifications. There are no third-party
+services, analytics, or runtime external requests.
+
+## Verification
+
+With the server running using the default test credentials (`moderator` /
+`test-password`), or the test environment variables set:
+
+```sh
+cargo test --offline --locked
+cargo clippy --offline --locked -- -D warnings
+python3 tests/live.py
+python3 tests/live_browser.py
+python3 tests/live_persistence.py
+python3 tests/smoke.py
+python3 tests/browser.py
+python3 tests/import_export.py
+python3 tests/persistence.py
+```
+
+`live.py` exercises isolation, independent repeat games, skipping inactive
+questions, late joins, latest-answer counting, all feedback outcomes, closed
+and stale-write rejection, role permissions, CSRF, empty games, immediate phase
+notifications, and the absence of per-answer phone broadcasts.
+
+`live_browser.py` uses installed Chromium in separate cookie contexts for the
+moderator and phones. It checks exact labels, no-reload updates, remembered
+identity, answer changes, rapid taps, a simulated Wi-Fi interruption, end-state
+join blocking, QR image loading, and narrow-screen layout. Screenshots are saved
+under `storage/`. `tests/cdp.py` is a small standard-library DevTools helper shared
+with the existing browser suite; no downloaded browser tooling is needed.
+
+`live_persistence.py` uses isolated temporary storage under `storage/` and kills
+the process abruptly twice to check WAL recovery, player identity, answers,
+ended status, and pre-restart polling cursors. Rust tests additionally check
+presence expiry/recovery, multiple correct options, snapshot stability, and
+absence of hidden correctness fields in open-question public payloads.
diff --git a/src/game.rs b/src/game.rs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3e3dce7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/game.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,398 @@
+use crate::{
+    App, html,
+    model::{self, Draft, Form, Quiz},
+    not_found, views,
+};
+use axum::{
+    body::to_bytes,
+    extract::Request,
+    http::{StatusCode, header},
+    response::{IntoResponse, Redirect, Response},
+};
+use rusqlite::{Connection, OptionalExtension, params};
+use serde_json::{Value, json};
+use std::time::Duration;
+
+pub fn initialize(db: &Connection) -> rusqlite::Result<()> {
+    db.execute_batch("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS games (
+        code TEXT PRIMARY KEY, quiz_id INTEGER NOT NULL, title TEXT NOT NULL,
+        questions TEXT NOT NULL, phase TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'waiting', position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
+        version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0);
+        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS players (
+        game TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES games(code), token TEXT NOT NULL, name TEXT NOT NULL,
+        seen INTEGER NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(game,token));
+        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS answers (
+        game TEXT NOT NULL, player TEXT NOT NULL, question INTEGER NOT NULL, choice INTEGER NOT NULL,
+        PRIMARY KEY(game,player,question), FOREIGN KEY(game,player) REFERENCES players(game,token));")
+}
+fn random(db: &Connection, bytes: i64) -> rusqlite::Result<String> {
+    db.query_row("SELECT lower(hex(randomblob(?)))", [bytes], |r| r.get(0))
+}
+pub fn create(db: &mut Connection, quiz: &Quiz) -> rusqlite::Result<Response> {
+    let questions: Vec<_> = model::QuizContents::from_quiz(quiz, model::questions(db, quiz.id)?)
+        .questions
+        .into_iter()
+        .filter(|q| q.active)
+        .collect();
+    let code = random(db, 5)?.to_uppercase();
+    db.execute(
+        "INSERT INTO games(code,quiz_id,title,questions) VALUES (?,?,?,?)",
+        params![
+            code,
+            quiz.id,
+            quiz.title,
+            serde_json::to_string(&questions).unwrap()
+        ],
+    )?;
+    Ok(Redirect::to(&format!("/moderate/games/{code}")).into_response())
+}
+struct Game {
+    title: String,
+    questions: Vec<Draft>,
+    phase: String,
+    position: usize,
+    version: i64,
+}
+fn load(db: &Connection, code: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<Option<Game>> {
+    db.query_row(
+        "SELECT title,questions,phase,position,version FROM games WHERE code=?",
+        [code],
+        |r| {
+            let raw: String = r.get(1)?;
+            Ok(Game {
+                title: r.get(0)?,
+                questions: serde_json::from_str(&raw).expect("saved questions"),
+                phase: r.get(2)?,
+                position: r.get(3)?,
+                version: r.get(4)?,
+            })
+        },
+    )
+    .optional()
+}
+fn player(db: &Connection, code: &str, token: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<Option<String>> {
+    db.query_row(
+        "SELECT name FROM players WHERE game=? AND token=?",
+        params![code, token],
+        |r| r.get(0),
+    )
+    .optional()
+}
+fn touch(db: &Connection, code: &str, token: &str) -> rusqlite::Result<bool> {
+    let returning: bool = db.query_row(
+        "SELECT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM players WHERE game=? AND token=? AND seen < unixepoch()-35)",
+        params![code, token],
+        |r| r.get(0),
+    )?;
+    db.execute(
+        "UPDATE players SET seen=unixepoch() WHERE game=? AND token=?",
+        params![code, token],
+    )?;
+    Ok(returning)
+}
+fn state(
+    db: &Connection,
+    code: &str,
+    token: &str,
+    moderator: bool,
+    g: &Game,
+    revision: u64,
+) -> rusqlite::Result<Value> {
+    let name = player(db, code, token)?;
+    let mut s = json!({"title":g.title,"phase":g.phase,"version":g.version,"revision":revision,"name":name,"total":g.questions.len()});
+    if moderator {
+        s["players"] = db
+            .query_row(
+                "SELECT count(*) FROM players WHERE game=? AND seen>=unixepoch()-35",
+                [code],
+                |r| r.get::<_, i64>(0),
+            )?
+            .into();
+    }
+    if g.phase == "open" || g.phase == "closed" {
+        // Unjoined browsers receive no question data. Correctness is never serialized while open.
+        if !moderator && name.is_none() {
+            return Ok(s);
+        }
+        let q = &g.questions[g.position];
+        let pick: Option<usize> = db
+            .query_row(
+                "SELECT choice FROM answers WHERE game=? AND player=? AND question=?",
+                params![code, token, g.position],
+                |r| r.get(0),
+            )
+            .optional()?;
+        s["position"] = g.position.into();
+        s["question"] = q.text.clone().into();
+        s["pick"] = json!(pick);
+        let mut options = Vec::new();
+        for (i, o) in q.options.iter().enumerate() {
+            let mut option = json!({"text":o.text});
+            if g.phase == "closed" {
+                option["correct"] = o.correct.into();
+                if moderator {
+                    option["count"] = db
+                        .query_row(
+                            "SELECT count(*) FROM answers WHERE game=? AND question=? AND choice=?",
+                            params![code, g.position, i],
+                            |r| r.get::<_, i64>(0),
+                        )?
+                        .into();
+                }
+            }
+            options.push(option);
+        }
+        s["options"] = options.into();
+        if moderator {
+            s["answers"] = db.query_row("SELECT count(*) FROM answers a JOIN players p ON p.game=a.game AND p.token=a.player WHERE a.game=? AND a.question=? AND p.seen>=unixepoch()-35", params![code,g.position], |r| r.get::<_,i64>(0))?.into();
+        } else if g.phase == "closed" {
+            s["result"] = match pick {
+                None => "No answer",
+                Some(i) if q.options[i].correct => "Correct!",
+                _ => "Wrong!",
+            }
+            .into();
+        }
+    }
+    Ok(s)
+}
+fn shell(code: &str, g: &Game, moderator: bool, token: &str, join: &str) -> String {
+    let e = views::escape;
+    let body = format!(
+        r#"<main class="live-main {}" id="live" data-moderator="{moderator}" data-base="{}" data-token="{}"><div class="live-heading"><span class="eyebrow">{} · LIVE QUIZ</span><h1>{}</h1></div><section id="live-content" aria-live="polite">Connecting…</section><section id="join-info" {}><p>Join the quiz on your phone</p><a class="join-link" href="{}">{}</a><img class="join-qr" src="/moderate/games/{code}/qr.svg" alt="QR code for the join link" width="240" height="240"></section><p id="live-status" role="status"></p><noscript>Enable JavaScript to join and follow the live quiz.</noscript></main><script src="/assets/live.js" defer></script>"#,
+        if moderator { "big-screen" } else { "phone" },
+        if moderator {
+            format!("/moderate/games/{code}")
+        } else {
+            format!("/play/{code}")
+        },
+        e(token),
+        if moderator { "BIG SCREEN" } else { "QUIZZY" },
+        e(&g.title),
+        if moderator && g.phase == "waiting" {
+            ""
+        } else {
+            "hidden"
+        },
+        e(join),
+        e(join)
+    );
+    // Public pages contain neither moderator tokens nor moderator navigation.
+    if moderator {
+        views::page(&g.title, &body, token)
+    } else {
+        format!(r#"<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{} · Quizzy</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/quizzy.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/app.css"></head><body>{}</body></html>"#,e(&g.title),body.replace(&format!("<img class=\"join-qr\" src=\"/moderate/games/{code}/qr.svg\" alt=\"QR code for the join link\" width=\"240\" height=\"240\">"), ""))
+    }
+}
+
+pub async fn handle(app: App, req: Request, moderator: bool) -> Response {
+    let path = req.uri().path().trim_end_matches('/').to_owned();
+    let parts: Vec<_> = path.split('/').collect();
+    let offset = if moderator { 3 } else { 2 };
+    if parts.len() < offset + 1 || parts.len() > offset + 2 {
+        return not_found();
+    }
+    let code = parts[offset].to_owned();
+    let action = parts.get(offset + 1).copied().unwrap_or("").to_owned();
+    let method = req.method().as_str().to_owned();
+    if !["GET", "POST", "HEAD"].contains(&method.as_str()) {
+        return StatusCode::METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED.into_response();
+    }
+    let query: Form =
+        serde_urlencoded::from_str(req.uri().query().unwrap_or("")).unwrap_or_default();
+    let since = query.get("since").and_then(|x| x.parse::<u64>().ok());
+    let host = req
+        .headers()
+        .get(header::HOST)
+        .and_then(|h| h.to_str().ok())
+        .unwrap_or("localhost:3000")
+        .to_owned();
+    let cookie = req
+        .headers()
+        .get(header::COOKIE)
+        .and_then(|h| h.to_str().ok())
+        .unwrap_or("")
+        .split(';')
+        .find_map(|part| part.trim().strip_prefix("quizzy_player="))
+        .filter(|v| v.len() == 64 && v.bytes().all(|b| b.is_ascii_hexdigit()))
+        .unwrap_or("")
+        .to_owned();
+    let form: Form = if method == "POST" {
+        let Ok(bytes) = to_bytes(req.into_body(), 8192).await else {
+            return StatusCode::PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE.into_response();
+        };
+        let Ok(form) = serde_urlencoded::from_bytes(&bytes) else {
+            return StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST.into_response();
+        };
+        form
+    } else {
+        Form::new()
+    };
+    if method == "POST"
+        && !form
+            .get("csrf")
+            .is_some_and(|t| !t.is_empty() && t == if moderator { &app.csrf } else { &cookie })
+    {
+        return (
+            StatusCode::FORBIDDEN,
+            "Invalid form token. Reload and try again.",
+        )
+            .into_response();
+    }
+    let mut changes = if moderator {
+        app.changes.subscribe()
+    } else {
+        app.phases.subscribe()
+    };
+    if action == "state" && method == "GET" && since == Some(*changes.borrow_and_update()) {
+        let _ = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(10), changes.changed()).await;
+    }
+    let result = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || -> rusqlite::Result<Response> {
+        let db = app.db.lock().expect("database lock");
+        let Some(mut g) = load(&db,&code)? else { return Ok(not_found()); };
+        let token = if cookie.is_empty() {random(&db,32)?} else {cookie.clone()};
+        let csrf = if moderator {app.csrf.as_str()} else {token.as_str()};
+        let join = format!("http://{host}/play/{code}");
+        if method == "GET" || method == "HEAD" {
+            if action.is_empty() {
+                let mut response = html(shell(&code,&g,moderator,csrf,&join));
+                if !moderator && cookie.is_empty() {
+                    response.headers_mut().insert(header::SET_COOKIE, format!("quizzy_player={token}; Path=/play; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Max-Age=31536000").parse().unwrap());
+                }
+                return Ok(response);
+            }
+            if action == "qr.svg" && moderator {
+                let Ok(qr) = qrcode::QrCode::new(join.as_bytes()) else {
+                    return Ok((StatusCode::BAD_REQUEST, "Host name is too long for a QR code").into_response());
+                };
+                let w = qr.width();
+                let mut svg = format!(r#"<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 {} {}"><rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="white"/><path fill="black" d=""#,w+8,w+8);
+                for y in 0..w { for x in 0..w { if qr[(x,y)] == qrcode::Color::Dark { svg.push_str(&format!("M{} {}h1v1h-1z",x+4,y+4)); } } }
+                svg.push_str("\"/></svg>");
+                return Ok(([(header::CONTENT_TYPE,"image/svg+xml")],svg).into_response());
+            }
+            if action != "state" { return Ok(not_found()); }
+            if !moderator && g.phase != "ended" && touch(&db,&code,&token)? { app.changes.send_modify(|v| *v+=1); }
+        } else {
+            match (moderator,action.as_str()) {
+                (false,"join") => {
+                    if g.phase == "ended" { return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"The quiz is over").into_response()); }
+                    let name = form.get("name").map(|s| s.trim()).unwrap_or("");
+                    if name.is_empty() || name.chars().count()>80 { return Ok((StatusCode::UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY,"Enter your name (1–80 characters).").into_response()); }
+                    db.execute("INSERT INTO players(game,token,name,seen) VALUES (?,?,?,unixepoch()) ON CONFLICT(game,token) DO UPDATE SET seen=unixepoch()",params![code,token,name])?;
+                }
+                (false,"answer") => {
+                    let position = form.get("position").and_then(|s| s.parse::<usize>().ok());
+                    let choice = form.get("choice").and_then(|s| s.parse::<usize>().ok());
+                    if g.phase != "open" || position != Some(g.position) || choice.is_none_or(|c| c >= g.questions[g.position].options.len()) || player(&db,&code,&token)?.is_none() {
+                        return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"This question is no longer open. Reconnecting…").into_response());
+                    }
+                    db.execute("INSERT INTO answers(game,player,question,choice) VALUES (?,?,?,?) ON CONFLICT(game,player,question) DO UPDATE SET choice=excluded.choice",params![code,token,g.position,choice.unwrap()])?;
+                    touch(&db,&code,&token)?;
+                }
+                (true,"action") => {
+                    if form.get("version").and_then(|s| s.parse::<i64>().ok()) != Some(g.version) { return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"The game has already moved on.").into_response()); }
+                    let command = form.get("command").map(String::as_str).unwrap_or("");
+                    match (g.phase.as_str(),command) {
+                        ("waiting","start") => g.phase = if g.questions.is_empty() {"ended"} else {"open"}.into(),
+                        ("open","finish") => g.phase="closed".into(),
+                        ("closed","next") if g.position+1<g.questions.len() => {g.position+=1; g.phase="open".into();},
+                        ("closed","end") if g.position+1==g.questions.len() => g.phase="ended".into(),
+                        _ => return Ok((StatusCode::CONFLICT,"Invalid game transition").into_response())
+                    }
+                    g.version+=1;
+                    db.execute("UPDATE games SET phase=?,position=?,version=? WHERE code=?",params![g.phase,g.position,g.version,code])?;
+                }
+                _ => return Ok(not_found())
+            }
+            app.changes.send_modify(|v| *v+=1);
+            if moderator { app.phases.send_replace(*app.changes.borrow()); }
+        }
+        let mut state = state(&db,&code,&token,moderator,&g,*app.changes.borrow())?;
+        state["cursor"] = if moderator { *app.changes.borrow() } else { *app.phases.borrow() }.into();
+        Ok(axum::Json(state).into_response())
+    }).await;
+    match result {
+        Ok(Ok(response)) => response,
+        error => {
+            eprintln!("Game request failed: {error:?}");
+            (
+                StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,
+                "Unable to load game. Please try again.",
+            )
+                .into_response()
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+#[cfg(test)]
+mod tests {
+    use super::*;
+
+    #[test]
+    fn snapshots_presence_and_private_payloads() {
+        let mut db = Connection::open_in_memory().unwrap();
+        model::initialize(&db).unwrap();
+        initialize(&db).unwrap();
+        let contents = model::QuizContents::parse(r#"{"title":"Test","questions":[
+            {"text":"Multiple correct","options":[{"text":"A","correct":true},{"text":"B","correct":true},{"text":"C"}]},
+            {"text":"Inactive","active":false,"options":[{"text":"A","correct":true},{"text":"B"}]}
+        ]}"#).unwrap();
+        let id = contents.insert(&mut db).unwrap();
+        let quiz = model::quiz(&db, id).unwrap().unwrap();
+        create(&mut db, &quiz).unwrap();
+        let code: String = db
+            .query_row("SELECT code FROM games", [], |r| r.get(0))
+            .unwrap();
+        // Editing/deleting source content must not alter an already-created game.
+        db.execute("DELETE FROM quizzes", []).unwrap();
+        let mut game = load(&db, &code).unwrap().unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(game.questions.len(), 1);
+        db.execute(
+            "INSERT INTO players VALUES (?, 'alice', 'Alice', unixepoch())",
+            [&code],
+        )
+        .unwrap();
+        db.execute(
+            "INSERT INTO players VALUES (?, 'bob', 'Bob', unixepoch()-40)",
+            [&code],
+        )
+        .unwrap();
+        db.execute("INSERT INTO answers VALUES (?, 'alice', 0, 1)", [&code])
+            .unwrap();
+        db.execute("INSERT INTO answers VALUES (?, 'bob', 0, 2)", [&code])
+            .unwrap();
+        game.phase = "open".into();
+        let public = state(&db, &code, "alice", false, &game, 1).unwrap();
+        assert!(public["options"][0].get("correct").is_none());
+        assert!(public.get("result").is_none());
+        assert!(
+            state(&db, &code, "stranger", false, &game, 1)
+                .unwrap()
+                .get("question")
+                .is_none()
+        );
+        let screen = state(&db, &code, "", true, &game, 1).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(screen["players"], 1);
+        assert_eq!(screen["answers"], 1);
+        assert!(touch(&db, &code, "bob").unwrap());
+        assert!(!touch(&db, &code, "bob").unwrap());
+        let screen = state(&db, &code, "", true, &game, 1).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(screen["players"], 2);
+        assert_eq!(screen["answers"], 2);
+        game.phase = "closed".into();
+        assert_eq!(
+            state(&db, &code, "alice", false, &game, 1).unwrap()["result"],
+            "Correct!"
+        );
+        assert_eq!(
+            state(&db, &code, "bob", false, &game, 1).unwrap()["result"],
+            "Wrong!"
+        );
+        let screen = state(&db, &code, "", true, &game, 1).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(screen["options"][0]["correct"], true);
+        assert_eq!(screen["options"][1]["correct"], true);
+        assert_eq!(screen["options"][1]["count"], 1);
+        assert_eq!(screen["options"][2]["count"], 1);
+    }
+}
